  "summary": "Four preprints in mid-November 2026 apply neural and likelihood-based reconstruction to Lyα, lensing, and galaxy-survey data.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is inverting noisy astrophysical observables into underlying matter or gas fields. One preprint uses a CNN to recover intergalactic medium column-density maps from KCWI Lyα emission cubes of z~2.3 protoclusters. Another trains deep networks on hydrodynamical simulations to infer cluster mass maps and subhalo substructure from HST optical imaging, matching CLASH lensing. A weak-lensing study extends beyond flexion with roulette amplitudes, where higher-order terms improve least-squares lens-mass reconstruction. A fourth develops a faster field-level likelihood for large-scale galaxy surveys, forecasting improved primordial non-Gaussianity constraints. What is new is the breadth of reconstruction targets, spanning simulation-trained inference and analytic or likelihood-based approaches, with the IGM work explicitly a proof of concept.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-18"
}
